## File regions

Every `<name>.tsx` file uses `#region` blocks in this order. Skip regions that do not apply; never reorder.

| Order | Region | When |
| ----- | ------ | ---- |
| 1 | `Types` | Props, variant prop types (imported from recipes), item interfaces (not context value types) |
| 2 | `Hooks` | File-local hooks not exported from `index.ts` |
| 3 | `Part` / `Parts` | Compound / closed component functions (not shorthand/closed compose) |
| 4 | `Shorthand` / `Closed` | Preset compose — after all parts (`FooShorthand` or closed `Foo`) |
| 5 | `Display Names` | All `displayName` assignments for the file — always last when any part sets `displayName` |

Context factory + value types live in [`<name>.context.tsx`](#context-file-namecontexttsx) — not a region in `<name>.tsx`. Do **not** add a `#region Variants` — `tv()` recipes live in `@pisagor/recipes`, not in component files.

### Do

- Use **`#region Part`** (singular) when the file exports **one** component function.
- Use **`#region Parts`** (plural) when the file exports **two or more** component functions.
- Use **`#region Shorthand`** when the file exports `FooShorthand` — place it **after** `#region Parts`, not inside it.
- Use **`#region Closed`** for closed multi-slot compose (`Foo` that wires private parts) — place it **after** `#region Parts`, not inside it. Parts stay file-private; do not barrel-export them.
- Use **`#region Display Names`** when any export sets `displayName` — place it **last**, after Parts / Shorthand / Closed. Include every assignment in declaration order (parts first, then shorthand/closed). Spell the region exactly `Display Names` (with a space) — not `DisplayNames`.
- Start at `Types` → `Part(s)` (skip Hooks when none).
- Put **`// #endregion` on the line immediately after** the region's last statement — no blank line before it.
- Put **one blank line between region blocks** — after `// #endregion`, before the next `// #region`.
- Follow [react.mdc → Component body order](../styleguides/react.mdc#component-body-order) inside each component function.

### Do not

- Do not add a `#region Variants` or call `tv()` in component packages — own recipes in `@pisagor/recipes`.
- Do not add an `Exports` region — public API belongs in `index.ts`.
- Do not add empty `#region` / `#endregion` pairs — skip regions that have no content.
- Do not keep a `#region Context` in `<name>.tsx` — use `<name>.context.tsx` instead.
- Do not declare `export type` / `export interface` props outside `#region Types` — keep every part props type in Types; Parts only contain component functions.

**Note:** Types region order is file-level type declaration order — not the same as [react.mdc → Props order](../styleguides/react.mdc#props-order) field groups.

Inside `Types`, when all apply: sub-element prop types → `{Name}ClassNames` → `{Name}VariantProps` → root props → public interface → preset interfaces (`AccordionItem`, …).

